1
00:00:00,273 --> 00:00:07,523
(Q31（单选）) I've been doing some research into what people in Britain think of doctors, the ones who work in general practice -

2
00:00:07,523 --> 00:00:14,041
the first call for medical care - and comparing this with the situation in a couple of other countries.

3
00:00:14,041 --> 00:00:18,928
I want to talk about the rationale behind what I decided to do.

4
00:00:18,928 --> 00:00:28,769
[跨国筹备] Now I had to set up my programme of research in three different countries so I approached postgraduates in my field in overseas departments,

5
00:00:28,769 --> 00:00:33,654
contacting them by email, to organize things for me at their end.

6
00:00:33,654 --> 00:00:43,122
I thought I would have trouble recruiting help but in fact everyone was very willing and sometimes their tutors got involved too.

7
00:00:43,122 --> 00:00:50,701
I had to give my helpers clear instructions about what kind of sample population I wanted them to use.

8
00:00:50,701 --> 00:00:59,271
[样本选择] I decided that people under 18 should be excluded because most of them are students or looking for their first job,

9
00:00:59,271 --> 00:01:05,466
and also I decided at this stage just to focus on men who were in employment,

10
00:01:05,466 --> 00:01:13,410
and set up something for people who didn't have jobs and for employed women later on as a separate investigation.

11
00:01:13,410 --> 00:01:19,966
[研究方法] I specifically wanted to do a questionnaire, and interviews with a focus group.

12
00:01:19,966 --> 00:01:28,124
With the questionnaire, rather than limiting it to one specific point, I wanted to include as much variety as possible.

13
00:01:28,124 --> 00:01:38,727
I know questionnaires are a very controlled way to do things but I thought I could do taped interviews later on to counteract the effects of this.

14
00:01:38,727 --> 00:01:50,094
And the focus group may also prove useful in future, by targeting subjects I can easily return to, as the participants tend to be more involved.

15
00:01:50,094 --> 00:01:53,199
So I'm just collating the results now.

16
00:01:53,199 --> 00:02:01,875
[初步结果] At the moment it looks as if, in the UK, despite the fact that newspapers continually report that people are unhappy with medical care,

17
00:02:01,875 --> 00:02:10,032
in fact it is mainly the third level of care, which takes place in hospitals, that they are worried about.

18
00:02:10,032 --> 00:02:23,293
Government reforms have been proposed at all levels and although their success is not guaranteed, long-term hospital care is in fact probably less of an issue than the media would have us believe.

19
00:02:23,293 --> 00:02:27,719
However, I've still got quite a bit of data to look at.

20
00:02:27,719 --> 00:02:38,627
[后续方向] Certainly I will need to do more far-reaching research than I had anticipated in order to establish if people want extra medical staff invested in the community,

21
00:02:38,627 --> 00:02:44,796
or if they want care to revert to fewer, but larger, key medical units.

22
00:02:44,796 --> 00:02:55,664
The solution may well be something that can be easily implemented by those responsible in local government, with central government support of course.

23
00:02:55,664 --> 00:02:59,703
[研究反馈] This first stage has proved very valuable though.

24
00:02:59,703 --> 00:03:09,648
I was surprised by how willing most of the subjects were to get involved in the project - I had expected some unwillingness to answer questions honestly.

25
00:03:09,648 --> 00:03:24,512
But I was taken aback and rather concerned that something I thought I'd set up very well didn't necessarily seem that way to everyone in my own department.

26
00:03:24,512 --> 00:03:32,146
(Q37（配对）) I thought you might also be interested in some of the problems I encountered in collecting my data.

27
00:03:32,146 --> 00:03:43,657
[🟢定位词： shopping in town = in the street, 上下义 。    Q37答案句B： pull out 退出= stop participating ，注意decide不能作为定位词，有可能替换/出现的但实为干扰的] There were odd cases that threw me - one of the subjects who I had approached while he was out shopping in town, decided to pull out when it came to the second round.

28
00:03:43,657 --> 00:03:49,983
It was a shame as it was someone who I would like to have interviewed more closely.

29
00:03:49,983 --> 00:03:58,140
(Q38) [🟢定位 first-year student =undergraduate。    Q37答案句F： no name be traceable = confidentiality] And one of the first-year students I interviewed wanted reassurance that no names would be traceable from the answers.

30
00:03:58,140 --> 00:04:06,383
I was so surprised, because they think nothing of telling you about themselves and their opinions in seminar groups!

31
00:04:06,383 --> 00:04:10,583
(Q39) [🟢定位： I work with = colleague, 解释型] Then, one of the people that I work with got a bit funny.

32
00:04:10,583 --> 00:04:21,532
[Q39答案句D：one minute ..., then..., in the end ... = keep changing mind] The questions were quite personal and one minute he said he'd do it, then the next day he wouldn't, and in the end he did do it.

33
00:04:21,532 --> 00:04:31,369
[Q39干扰项E：angry， 对象反了，要angry也得是Shona对采访对象] It's hard not to get angry in that situation but I tried to keep focused on the overall picture in order to stay calm.

34
00:04:31,369 --> 00:04:38,852
(Q40) [🟢定位词：teacher=tutor] The most bizarre case was a telephone interview I did with a teacher at a university in France.

35
00:04:38,852 --> 00:04:51,334
[Q40答案句C：wouldn't tell = refuse to] He answered all my questions in great detail- but then when I asked how much access he had to dangerous substances he wouldn't tell me exactly what his work involved.

36
00:04:51,334 --> 00:04:53,834
It's a real eye-opener...

